  "zld_mandate_rules": [
    "Zero Liquid Discharge (ZLD) is mandatory for textile dyeing and bleaching clusters in environmentally sensitive basins (e.g. Tirupur, Noyyal river basin, Cauvery, Ganga basin).",
    "100% of treated effluent must be recovered as high-quality permeate (RO Permeate TDS < 100 mg/L) and reused in dyeing process baths.",
    "Zero untreated or treated liquid effluent is allowed to cross unit boundary walls or enter storm drains.",
    "Dry salts (NaCl / Na2SO4) produced by MEE/ATFD must be either refined for textile process reuse or disposed at Authorized Hazardous Waste TSDF Facilities."
  ]
